    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d183">

                <pb facs="0405" n="385" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg385"/>

                <head>Lord Lyons to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">British Legation,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-07-03"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 3, 1863. </date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to submit to you a protest
                    made by Mr. E. J. Locke, master of the brig Isabella Thompson, of Halifax, Nova
                    Scotia, against the capture of his ship by the United States vessel-of-war
                    United States.</p>
                <p>I shall be much obliged if you will return the protest to me after taking
                    cognizance of it.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with high consideration, sir, your most obedient, humble
                    servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>LYONS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d183-a1.xml" xpointer="d183-a1"/>
            </div>
